[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  The Copper Finch breathes. Rain drums against the shutters. Copper lamps 
  throw wavering pools across scarred oak. Mara Venn looks up from the iron 
  reliquary. Her charcoal coat rustles as she leans back. Fingers tap the table 
  once, twice. "Kael." A nod. No smile. "The Ash Gate." She gestures at the 
  rain-smeared window — beyond it, the dark seam of the city wall, and the gate 
  that stays shut. "Old Bram's corpse washed up against the western pier at 
  dawn. The gatekeepers found him floating. No wounds. No blood. Just... 
  empty." She lets that hang. "Gate hasn't opened since. The lock mechanism is 
  seized solid — like it's been welded from the inside. No one gets through. No 
  one gets out." Her eyes drop to the reliquary. A bronze pin glints in the 
  lamplight. "I've been sitting here asking myself who'd want the Ash Gate 
  sealed. And why now." She looks back at you. "You're the one who knew Bram. 
  What do you make of it?" 

