[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  You reach into your pack and pull out the brass compass — its face warm, its 
  chain familiar. You hold it across the table to Mara. She looks at it. Her 
  hand hovers over it. Then she draws back. "No." The word lands flat. She 
  shakes her head once, a tight motion. "That's not a trinket, Kael. That 
  compass has been in your family longer than the Ash Gate's been shut. You 
  don't hand that to someone you've known for two hours over a tavern table." 
  She pushes her chair back an inch. The legs scrape the floorboards. "Keep it. 
  Use it. If we're going to figure out what happened to Bram and why that gate 
  is sealed, you'll need your wits about you — and that thing is part of your 
  wits." She taps the reliquary instead. The bronze pin trembles. "This box, 
  though. This box I need to open. And I need your eyes on it before I pull 
  that pin. Will you look at it with me?" 

