  Mara's fingers go still on the reliquary. She looks at you — a long, 
  measuring look — then reaches into an inner pocket of her coat. Her hand 
  emerges with something dark. She places it on the table between you with a 
  soft *click*. It's a finger-length key carved from obsidian — volcanic glass, 
  polished to a mirror sheen. The head is shaped like a crescent, and a fine 
  groove runs along its full length, catching the lamplight like a vein of 
  captured shadow. "I was going to hold onto that until I trusted you more." 
  Her voice is low, flat. "But you paid. You asked about Bram. You didn't 
  flinch at the scar." She pushes it an inch closer. "That key opens a lockbox 
  in the Ash Gate archive. The archive where Lysander Vex worked before someone 
  burned his rooms. I found it in the ashes — the key, not the box. The box is 
  still there, hidden behind a loose stone in the west wall." She leans back, 
  arms crossed. "If you're going to carry it, carry it carefully. That key is 
  the only one I know of. Lose it, and whatever's in that box stays buried." 
  The rain hammers the shutters. The reliquary sits between you, its bronze pin 
  gleaming — one pull away from violence. Your fingers close around the 
  obsidian. It's cool, smooth, heavier than it looks. What do you do with it? 
