[1m[95m[NARRATION][0m 
  The rain has softened to a drizzle by the time you round the last corner. The 
  Ash Gate looms ahead, a cracked black monument to silence. But you're not 
  alone. A figure stands at the base of the arch, hooded against the drizzle, a 
  leather satchel slung across one shoulder. Young — early twenties, maybe — 
  with a sharp jaw and darker skin, rain beading on the exposed bridge of her 
  nose. She's been waiting. Not pacing. Not sheltering. Just *waiting*, still 
  as the stone behind her. She sees you coming and doesn't flinch. Doesn't 
  reach for a weapon. Just watches you close the distance with calm, appraising 
  eyes. You stop a few paces from her. Introduce yourself. A pause. Then she 
  pulls back her hood. Dark hair, cropped short. A scar like a thin white 
  thread cutting through her left eyebrow. She offers a faint, wry smile. 
  "Sable Quill." Her voice is low, rough at the edges — a smoker's voice, or a 
  screamer's, or both. "I was told an elf with a brass compass would come to 
  this gate before the new moon. Paid good silver for the tip." She tilts her 
  head, studying you. "Didn't think you'd show up with the Watch at your heels 
  and a scorch mark on your coat, though. You make a habit of setting off 
  explosions before breakfast?" 

